      "page_title": "Logging, Tracing and Test Types",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Q42. How do logging, tracing and correlation IDs help debug a production API?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "A ==correlation ID== is one ID stamped on every log line of a request.",
            "The gateway makes it, or reuses the client's `X-Request-ID`.",
            "Pass it to every downstream call and put it in the response.",
            "Use **structured** JSON logs so you can search by ID.",
            "Tracing adds spans: which hop was slow."
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "rid = headers.get('X-Request-ID')",
            "rid = rid or uuid4().hex",
            "log.info('paid', rid=rid)",
            "call(url, headers={'X-Request-ID': rid})"
          ]
        },
