      "page_title": "URL Shortener, Rate Limits and Checkout Design",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Q47. How would you design a URL shortener API?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Expose one ==create== endpoint and one ==redirect== endpoint. Map a short code to a long URL in a key-value store.",
            "`POST /links` returns **201** with the code; `GET /{code}` answers a **302** redirect",
            "Generate the code from a counter in ==base62==, or a random 7-char string",
            "Use 301 to cache forever; use 302 if you count clicks",
            "Cache hot codes in Redis; reads outnumber writes about 100:1"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "POST /links {\"url\": \"https://a.io/x\"}",
            "201 {\"code\": \"aZ3k9\"}",
            "GET /aZ3k9",
            "302 Location: https://a.io/x"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Choice",
            "Option",
            "Trade-off"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Code",
              "Counter + base62",
              "No collisions"
            ],
            [
              "Code",
              "Random 7 chars",
              "Retry on clash"
