        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Q50. How would you design a real-time notification API (WebSockets vs SSE vs polling)?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Pick the lightest transport that fits. Use ==SSE== for one-way server pushes, ==WebSockets== for two-way chat, and ==polling== as the simple fallback.",
            "SSE runs over plain HTTP and auto-reconnects with `Last-Event-ID`",
            "WebSockets keep a persistent socket, which is harder to scale and load-balance",
            "Short polling wastes requests; long polling holds one open until data arrives",
            "Fan out through Redis pub/sub or a broker so any node can push"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "GET /events",
            "Accept: text/event-stream",
            "id: 7",
            "data: {\"type\": \"shipped\"}"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "hero": "apigateway",
      "subtitle": "Design interview Q&A"
